Subject: [PATCH 286/310] Spatiand: video decoded by Spatiand's FFmpeg on
 VA-API

SpatiandVideoDecoder takes VaapiVideoDecoder's place in the GPU process: the pipeline's frame
pool allocates its buffers as VA surfaces through VaapiWrapper, FFmpeg decodes each picture into
one (its get_buffer2, on VaapiWrapper's display), and the frame goes to the compositor with
nothing copied. H.264, HEVC (8 and 10 bit), VP8, VP9 and AV1, as far as the GPU decodes them.
